Sylvia, the answer is no. The mail archive was never in scope for the Corva=
ntis migration, because it was never in Docuvault. It is a separate continu=
ous journal archive and it goes back to March 2008 without a break.<br />
<br />
It has everything.<br />
<br />
The production index is attached. The material findings, in order:<br />
<br />
April 6, 2011. Roland Ashcombe to Dana Truscott, copying Bernard Kilcoyne, =
Owen Radcliffe and Marguerite Okonkwo. VAA's formal written recommendation =
against deleting Section 09 05 61, with the letter attached on our letterhe=
ad. It states the 92 to 96% RH readings, predicts adhesive breakdown and li=
fting in eight to fifteen years, and says VAA will issue the ASI only on wr=
itten owner direction accepting responsibility.<br />
<br />
May 17, 2011. Dana Truscott to Roland Ashcombe, copying Kilcoyne, Radcliffe=
 and Okonkwo, with a signed directive on Ardsley letterhead attached. Ardsl=
ey directs the deletion, accepts the $347,900 credit and the 18 days, state=
s that the deletion is owner-directed and made over VAA's written recommend=
ation, states that Ardsley relied on Prewitt Building Science, and accepts =
responsibility for future flooring performance issues arising from slab moi=
sture.<br />
<br />
May 19, 2011. ASI-031, issued by Marguerite Okonkwo, deleting Section 09 05=
 61 on the Owner's written direction, with the owner-direction language on =
the face of the ASI.<br />
<br />
The full 2011 sequence is twelve messages plus the October 2010 specificati=
on transmittal, with nine attachments, all with intact original headers.<br=
 />
<br />
One caution for anyone searching. Project number 632588 returns two project=
s. Before the 2013 numbering consolidation the Iselin studio ran its own si=
x digit series, and 632588 in that series is the Meridian Health Partners a=
mbulatory center in Edison, which is a completely different job. The consol=
idation notice is attached so you can tell them apart. Ours is the Culver C=
ity series.
